    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What is NOT serving today",
      "items": [
        "Lexical BM25 arm + RetrievalFabric orchestrator: NOT PORTED to syllabai-v2 — the Java fabric was unwired by design (zero consumers, T-C13) and the v2 port serves the KG + vector arms directly (verified: no bm25/fabric module at d07267a)",
        "Reranking is interface-only in v2 as in core: the default is NoReranker (v0 no-op) until a benchmark promotes a reranker",
        "No serving behavior was lost at the cutover: every SERVING node here has a pin-verified v2 implementation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Truth boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The authoritative KG is canonical curriculum truth — retrieval-derived graph signals (Local Intelligence Layer) are PROPOSED and appear nowhere in serving",
        "Serving retrieval is NOT PDF→chunks→embeddings→vector DB→LLM: it is curriculum-scope-gated hybrid retrieval (KG + vector) fused rank-only, capped, and refused deterministically when nothing survives",
        "A parsed paper-question identity that binds zero validated anchors refuses deterministically (fail-open guard) — telemetry separates deterministic-paper-refusal from the grounding-gate refusal (D2)",
        "Working memory (prior turns, s139) and the cross-session episodic digest (s140) enter the assembled context — learner overlay, never canonical truth",
        "LLMs generate from the assembled context only — they never mark answers and never own curriculum truth",
        "Every citation resolves from surviving evidence items; there is no free-floating claim path. The sufficiency→generator edge is intentionally unlabeled: admission-on-pass is the gate's contract, refusal is documented here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Sources",
      "items": [
        "All 10 nodes live in syllabai-v2 apps/api (TypeScript port of record), pinned at d07267ae3d57974c202bf2f4141b9a3ba00a8ee8",
        "KaRAG pipeline contract (intent → KG context → hybrid retrieval → fusion → rerank → grounded generation → citations) is preserved 1:1 from the frozen Java core (port headers cite syllabai-core @ 6cad6ef)",
        "The v2 port drops the unwired Java arms — this diagram shrank from 12 to 10 nodes at the 2026-10-21 refresh"
      ]
    }
